<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a flighted conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A flighted conveyor is a belt conveyor with raised cleats, flights, or partitions bonded to the belt surface at regular intervals. The flights prevent product from sliding backward on inclines, allowing the conveyor to move bulk, granular, and small items up steep inclines. Sidewall belts and bucket designs reach fully vertical lifts.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is the difference between flighted and scoop conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Flighted conveyors use flat or angled cleats to prevent rollback on inclines. Scoop conveyors use enclosed bucket-shaped containers that fully retain product, including on vertical lifts. Scoops protect fragile products better but cost more and have lower throughput than cleated belts.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What incline angle can a flighted conveyor handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Standard cleats handle moderate to steep inclines. Sidewall cleated belts handle steep and vertical lifts, and Continental rates its FLEXOWELL sidewall system for any angle from 0° to 90°. Scoop and bucket conveyors handle very steep and vertical lifts. The maximum angle depends on product characteristics, free-flowing products need taller flights and lower angles, while cohesive products tolerate steeper angles with shorter flights.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">Are flighted conveyors available in food-grade designs?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Yes. Food-grade versions use polyurethane or silicone belts made from compounds that meet the applicable FDA food-contact regulation, with integrally molded flights, stainless steel frames, washdown-rated motors, and tool-free belt removal for cleaning. See <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/sanitary/">sanitary conveyors</a> for design details.</p>

</div>
